77
00:04:02.148 --> 00:04:05.113
Intuition: a restaurant menu and the order slip.

78
00:04:05.393 --> 00:04:08.785
An API is a restaurant's menu plus its order slips:

79
00:04:09.065 --> 00:04:12.863
The menu (the contract) tells customers what they can order and how.

80
00:04:13.143 --> 00:04:20.204
Once it's printed and in customers' hands, you can add dishes, but renaming or removing one confuses regulars.

81
00:04:20.484 --> 00:04:27.887
An order slip with a number (the idempotency key) means that if a waiter brings the same slip twice, the kitchen cooks it once.

82
00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.556
Is my table's order still what I think it is?

83
00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:35.209
(the ETag) stops you from cancelling a dish the kitchen has already served.

84
00:04:36.559 --> 00:04:43.023
A clear reason when something can't be done (the error model), such as Paneer is sold out; try Mushroom, beats No.

