00:31:13.673 --> 00:31:16.766
Sequence: happy path, idempotent order creation.

606
00:31:17.046 --> 00:31:19.841
The sequence diagram walks through it step by step.

607
00:31:20.121 --> 00:31:25.070
App to App: key = UUID for this checkout attempt (persisted locally).

608
00:31:25.350 --> 00:31:26.481
App to OS:

609
00:31:26.761 --> 00:31:31.881
POST or api or v1 or orders, Idempotency-Key k1, body B.

610
00:31:32.161 --> 00:31:33.313
OS to DB:

611
00:31:33.593 --> 00:31:38.009
INSERT idempotencyrecord(customer, k1, hash(B), INPROGRESS).

612
00:31:38.289 --> 00:31:41.830
DB to OS: inserted (unique on customer+key).

613
00:31:42.110 --> 00:31:46.590
OS to OS: validate cart, price, serviceability, reserve stock...

614
00:31:46.870 --> 00:31:48.022
OS to DB:

615
00:31:48.302 --> 00:31:55.427
INSERT order + items + outbox, UPDATE idempotencyrecord, then COMPLETED (201, body).

616
00:31:55.707 --> 00:31:56.710
OS to App:

617
00:31:56.990 --> 00:32:03.390
201 Created, Location or api or v1 or orders or ord9, ETag 1.

618
00:32:07.240 --> 00:32:11.443
Sequence: failure path, timeout, retry and a concurrent duplicate.

619
00:32:11.723 --> 00:32:14.517
The sequence diagram walks through it step by step.

620
00:32:14.797 --> 00:32:15.992
App to OS1:

621
00:32:16.272 --> 00:32:18.811
POST or orders, key k1, body B.

622
00:32:19.091 --> 00:32:20.499
OS1 to DB:

623
00:32:20.779 --> 00:32:24.085
INSERT idempotencyrecord(k1, INPROGRESS).

624
00:32:24.365 --> 00:32:27.864
App to App: client timeout at 5 s (outcome unknown).

625
00:32:28.144 --> 00:32:32.240
App to OS2: retry POST or orders, key k1, body B.

626
00:32:32.520 --> 00:32:33.885
OS2 to DB:

627
00:32:34.165 --> 00:32:38.347
INSERT idempotencyrecord(k1), then unique violation.

628
00:32:38.627 --> 00:32:39.992
OS2 to DB:

629
00:32:40.272 --> 00:32:42.661
SELECT record k1, then INPROGRESS.

630
00:32:42.941 --> 00:32:44.072
OS2 to App:

631
00:32:44.352 --> 00:32:46.784
409 Conflict, Retry-After:

632
00:32:47.064 --> 00:32:49.133
2, code IDEMPOTENCYINPROGRESS.

633
00:32:49.413 --> 00:32:55.365
OS1 to DB: order committed, record k1, then COMPLETED (201, body).

634
00:32:55.645 --> 00:32:59.635
App to OS2: retry after 2 s, key k1, body B.

635
00:32:59.915 --> 00:33:01.280
OS2 to DB:

636
00:33:01.560 --> 00:33:04.803
SELECT record k1, then COMPLETED, hash matches.

637
00:33:05.083 --> 00:33:06.213
OS2 to App:

638
00:33:06.493 --> 00:33:11.528
201 Created (replayed, identical body), Idempotent-Replayed: true.

639
00:33:11.808 --> 00:33:13.003
App to OS2:

640
00:33:13.283 --> 00:33:15.821
POST or orders, key k1, body B'.

641
00:33:16.101 --> 00:33:17.232
OS2 to App:

642
00:33:17.512 --> 00:33:20.307
422 IDEMPOTENCYKEYREUSED.

643
00:33:24.157 --> 00:33:24.903
Note:

644
00:33:25.183 --> 00:33:27.957
What the system guarantees after this failure path.

645
00:33:28.237 --> 00:33:36.258
Exactly one order per (customer, idempotency key), no matter how many retries arrive, on how many pods, or how concurrently.

646
00:33:36.538 --> 00:33:39.589
Retries receive the original response byte for byte.

647
00:33:39.869 --> 00:33:45.309
A reused key with a different body is rejected instead of silently returning the wrong order.

648
00:33:46.659 --> 00:33:49.155
State: idempotency record lifecycle.

649
00:33:49.435 --> 00:33:50.779
Here is the diagram.

