00:54:49.360 --> 00:54:50.811
ADR-021:

977
00:54:51.091 --> 00:54:55.656
URI major versions, additive evolution, contract-first governance.

978
00:54:55.936 --> 00:54:56.853
Context.

979
00:54:57.133 --> 00:55:03.619
Mobile app versions live 12 to 18 months, and 400 plus sellers integrate with our APIs.

980
00:55:03.899 --> 00:55:06.821
Unreviewed changes broke clients twice last year.

981
00:55:08.171 --> 00:55:09.046
Decision.

982
00:55:09.326 --> 00:55:14.531
(1) Public and seller APIs use a URI major version (/v1).

983
00:55:14.811 --> 00:55:23.003
Within a major version, only additive changes are allowed, and clients must be tolerant readers (unknown fields and enum values).

984
00:55:23.283 --> 00:55:26.526
(2) Specs are OpenAPI-first in the service repo:

985
00:55:26.806 --> 00:55:36.299
Spectral rules (idempotency headers, Problem Details, kebab-case paths, keyset pagination) and oasdiff breaking-change checks gate every PR.

986
00:55:36.579 --> 00:55:49.081
(3) Deprecations carry Deprecation, Sunset and Link headers, are metered per app version, and go through brownouts before 410 Gone, with a minimum 6-month window for public APIs.

987
00:55:49.361 --> 00:56:05.723
(4) Seller events are delivered as signed webhooks (HMAC-SHA256, timestamp tolerance of 5 min), at least once, with a stable event id, and retried for ~72 h before being dead-lettered with notification.

988
00:56:07.073 --> 00:56:08.097
Consequences.

989
00:56:08.377 --> 00:56:11.364
(+) Breaking changes can't merge accidentally.

990
00:56:11.644 --> 00:56:15.569
(+) SDKs are generated for Flutter, Angular and sellers.

991
00:56:15.849 --> 00:56:22.100
(minus ) Spec-first slows prototyping, so allow x-experimental endpoints behind feature flags.

992
00:56:22.380 --> 00:56:27.073
(minus ) Running two major versions doubles the test surface during migrations.

993
00:56:27.353 --> 00:56:40.495
Revisit when: seller integrations need finer-grained evolution (consider date-based versions per API key) or the number of client teams makes GraphQL federation attractive for the customer apps.

