1167
01:03:03.761 --> 01:03:04.700
Security.

1168
01:03:04.980 --> 01:03:06.644
Authorization per resource.

1169
01:03:06.924 --> 01:03:17.868
Every lookup is scoped by the authenticated principal (WHERE customerid =:me), which prevents IDOR, the top API vulnerability class (OWASP API1:

1170
01:03:18.148 --> 01:03:20.367
Broken Object Level Authorization).

1171
01:03:20.647 --> 01:03:25.959
Opaque, non-sequential IDs, and 404 for resources the caller can't see.

1172
01:03:26.239 --> 01:03:40.148
Input limits: max body size, max array lengths, max page size, strict JSON parsing (reject unknown fields on writes if you want strictness, or ignore them if you want tolerance, but decide explicitly).

1173
01:03:40.428 --> 01:03:45.143
Mass assignment: request DTOs contain only client-settable fields.

1174
01:03:45.423 --> 01:03:47.641
Never bind requests straight to entities.

1175
01:03:48.991 --> 01:03:55.071
Idempotency keys are scoped per client, so they can't be used to read another client's replayed responses.

1176
01:03:55.351 --> 01:03:56.546
Cursors are signed.

1177
01:03:56.826 --> 01:04:01.263
They leak nothing sensitive and can't be forged to skip authorization filters.

