01:05:51.391 --> 01:05:56.233
Idempotency adds roughly one extra insert and one update per mutation.

1224
01:05:56.513 --> 01:06:06.348
At ~850 per second peak that's negligible next to the order write itself, and it's far cheaper than one day of duplicate-refund reconciliation.

1225
01:06:06.628 --> 01:06:17.060
Keyset pagination turns deep-page queries from O(offset) into O(limit), often the single largest DB CPU saving for history screens.

1226
01:06:17.340 --> 01:06:20.540
Payload trimming reduces egress (Ch 02:

1227
01:06:20.820 --> 01:06:24.639
10 times differences are common) and serialization CPU.

1228
01:06:24.919 --> 01:06:32.151
Generated SDKs cost some CI time but save integration support hours for 400 plus sellers.

